<%# Complex template testing multiple helpers together %>
<%
  # Simulate data from a web application
  title = "Invoice #12345"
  customer_name = "John Doe & Associates"
  items = [
    { name: "Web Development", price: "$5,000", description: "Building <strong>awesome</strong> websites" },
    { name: "Consulting", price: "$2,500", description: "Strategic <em>planning</em> and advice" },
    { name: "Support Package", price: "$1,200/month", description: "24/7 <em>premium</em> support" }
  ]

  footer_html = <<~HTML
    <p><strong>Terms:</strong> Payment due within 30 days.</p>
    <p>For questions, visit <a href="https://example.com">our website</a>.</p>
  HTML

  company_info_md = <<~MD
    ## Company Information
    **Acme Corporation**
    123 Main Street
    _Anytown, USA 12345_
  MD
%>

= <%= escape_typst(title) %>

== Customer
Name: <%= escape_typst(customer_name) %>

== Invoice Items

<% items.each_with_index do |item, index| %>
*Item <%= index + 1 %>*: <%= escape_typst(item[:name]) %>

Price: <%= escape_typst(item[:price]) %>

Description: <%= html_to_typst(item[:description]) %>

<% end %>

== Company Details

<%= markdown_to_typst(company_info_md) %>

== Terms and Conditions

<%= html_to_typst(footer_html) %>

---

_Document generated on <%= Time.now.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") %>_

#pagebreak()

== Testing URL Encoding

Visit: `<%= url_encode("https://example.com/path?name=John Doe&id=123") %>`

== Appendix: External Content

<% appendix_path = File.join(__dir__, "../fixtures/sample.md") %>
<%= include_markdown(appendix_path) %>

This complex template demonstrates real-world usage combining multiple helpers:
- Text escaping for user-generated content
- HTML to Typst conversion for rich text
- Markdown to Typst for formatted content
- URL encoding for links
- Including external Markdown files
- ERB loops and conditionals
